#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/db/structured_conditionals.rst:3
msgid "The boolean structure system"
msgstr "The boolean structure system"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/db/structured_conditionals.rst:6
msgid "Intro"
msgstr "Intro"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/db/structured_conditionals.rst:8
msgid ""
"This feature helps extension authors to edit SQL queries in an easy and "
"quick way without the need to parse the SQL queries, most likely, using "
"regex and complex text editing. Instead of a single string, this allows "
"editing the WHERE clause in an SQL query by adding, removing and editing php "
"arrays. Using this method, finding the portion of the query to edit should "
"be much more straightforward."
msgstr ""
"This feature helps extension authors to edit SQL queries in an easy and "
"quick way without the need to parse the SQL queries, most likely, using "
"regex and complex text editing. Instead of a single string, this allows "
"editing the WHERE clause in an SQL query by adding, removing and editing php "
"arrays. Using this method, finding the portion of the query to edit should "
"be much more straightforward."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/db/structured_conditionals.rst:11
msgid ""
"If done correctly, incompatibilities between extensions that use the same "
"SQL query can be averted. Where a regex match could easly force the author "
"into making very complex matches. With this, finding and replacing the "
"content is just tree-like transversal as they are only arrays. Compatibility "
"between extensions becomes much easier."
msgstr ""
"If done correctly, incompatibilities between extensions that use the same "
"SQL query can be averted. Where a regex match could easly force the author "
"into making very complex matches. With this, finding and replacing the "
"content is just tree-like transversal as they are only arrays. Compatibility "
"between extensions becomes much easier."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/db/structured_conditionals.rst:13
msgid ""
"Althought this will definitely reduce the probability of inter-"
"incompatibilities between extensions, it is not magic. This is just a tool "
"that helps solving the same issue."
msgstr ""
"Althought this will definitely reduce the probability of inter-"
"incompatibilities between extensions, it is not magic. This is just a tool "
"that helps solving the same issue."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/db/structured_conditionals.rst:17
msgid "Main use-case ideals"
msgstr "Main use-case ideals"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/db/structured_conditionals.rst:19
msgid "To flexibly the build of the WHERE clause in SQL queries"
msgstr "To flexibly the build of the WHERE clause in SQL queries"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/db/structured_conditionals.rst:20
msgid ""
"To ease, simplify and prevent errors when doing SQL query editing by phpBB's "
"extensions"
msgstr ""
"To ease, simplify and prevent errors when doing SQL query editing by phpBB's "
"extensions"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/db/structured_conditionals.rst:23
msgid "Why not..."
msgstr "Why not..."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/db/structured_conditionals.rst:25
msgid ""
"Doctrine dbal -> The issue with Doctrine dbal is that its query builder is "
"not ready for the 2nd major use case listed above. There is no way of "
"altering an SQL query. If you want to alter something, you have to rebuild "
"the whole SQL query."
msgstr ""
"Doctrine dbal -> The issue with Doctrine dbal is that its query builder is "
"not ready for the 2nd major use case listed above. There is no way of "
"altering an SQL query. If you want to alter something, you have to rebuild "
"the whole SQL query."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/db/structured_conditionals.rst:26
msgid ""
"Linq -> I didn't know the assistance of Linq until today. From what I "
"searched, not only it has the same issue as Doctrine, while also its "
"interface is unnecessarily complex for the common folk who just wants to "
"change a small amount of information."
msgstr ""
"Linq -> I didn't know the assistance of Linq until today. From what I "
"searched, not only it has the same issue as Doctrine, while also its "
"interface is unnecessarily complex for the common folk who just wants to "
"change a small amount of information."

